  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dance music of the Dubrovnik coast, the Konavle valley and the Pelješac peninsula, played on the lijerica, a small pear-shaped three-string bowed lira held upright on the knee, whose player keeps time by stamping his foot. Its best-known dance is the linđo, a couple dance of the poskočica type whose figures are called out in rhymed commands by a dance leader (kolovođa).",
